# Pytest

- TDD: failing test before production code. Cover the sad path.
- `@pytest.mark.django_db` (or module `pytestmark`) when touching the database.
- Shared fixtures in `tests/conftest.py` (`user`, `staff_user`, `auth_client`).
  Factory Boy is not installed — add it per product if a model needs it.
- List views and endpoints get a `django_assert_num_queries` guard.
- Test behavior and HTTP/status/side effects, not Django internals.
- Keep tests hermetic: no `.env`, no clock, no network. Settings module is
  `core.settings.test`; Django deprecation warnings are errors.
- Run with `.venv/bin/pytest`.

See skill: `pytest-django-patterns`.
